markers.text:
Member of provincial
congresses, 1775-1776;
lieutenant colonel of
militia in Revolution;
Congressman, 1795-99. Grave
is 7 miles S.E.

Congressman from New York,
1821-39; House leader for
Jackson & Van Buren;
minister to Russia;
merchant. Was born in this
town, 1786.

President, N.C. Secession
Convention, 1861-1862;
Congressman, 1816-1827;
legislator. His grave is
three miles north.

Governor, 1824-1827;
Attorney General of N.C.;
Congressman. His home was
400 yds. W.

Lt. Col. in War of 1812;
state senator, 1835-52;
pres. Roanoke Navigation Co.
& Weldon & Portsmouth R.R.
Grave is 2 blks. S.

United States Senator from
Missouri, 1821-1851;
Congressman; author;
Jacksonian Democratic
leader; was born, 1782, in
this neighborhood.

Governor, 1845-1849;
Secretary of the Navy;
United States Senator; Whig
nominee for Vice-President
in 1852. His home stands 150
yds. W.

Member Congress, 1855-57;
Confederate Senator;
President State Convention,
1865; Justice N.C. Supreme
Court, 1865-78. Birthplace
was 2 mi. S.E.

Meeting house by 1761;
Meeting recognized, 1773;
Preparative Meeting, 1779; &
Monthly Meeting, 1793.

Black legislator & orator;
member 1868 convention; 
a founder of Republican Party & Union League in N.C. Home was 1 block W.

Colonel of black N.C.
regiment in war with Spain;
edited Raleigh Gazette;
legislator. Home was 25 ft.
W.

Four times Governor;
Revolutionary officer;
congressman. Grave is 9 1/2
miles north.

Lieutenant General, C.S.A.;
Supt. N.C. Military
Institute in Charlotte;
Davidson College professor;
Editor, "The Land We Love."
Grave is here.

U.S. Senator, 1954-1974;
led Senate Watergate
Committee, 1973-1974;
judge. His law office
was one block west.

Confederate captain;
legislator; member of
conventions of 1868, '75;
conservative leader in
Reconstruction period. His
home was 100 ft. S.

Governor, 1845-1849;
Secretary of the Navy;
United States Senator; Whig
nominee for Vice-President
in 1852. His birthplace is 3
mi. E.

Lutheran. A precursor of
Lenoir-Rhyne College;
burned, 1935. Church now on site 1 block south.

Physician; innovator in treatment of tuberculosis. Served n Europe, WWI;
operated a sanatorium 
here, 1908-1918.
